---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const resumeHref = "/resume";
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Tejas Kabra" description="About Tejas Kabra, an electrical engineering student at Texas A&M.">
  <section class="court-section border-b hairline py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="shell max-w-5xl">
      <p class="eyebrow text-signal">About</p>
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
        <h1 class="text-6xl font-semibold leading-[0.92] tracking-[-0.065em] md:text-8xl">
          Hi, I’m Tejas.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-8 text-xl leading-9 text-ink/72 md:text-2xl md:leading-10">
          I’m an Electrical Engineering student at Texas A&amp;M focused on embedded systems,
          PCB design, telemetry, power electronics, and robotics.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="bg-signal px-6 py-4 technical-label text-[0.74rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-panel transition-transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:bg-[#ff824f]" href={resumeHref}>
          View resume
        </a>
        <a class="border border-ink/20 px-6 py-4 technical-label text-[0.74rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors hover:border-signal hover:text-signal" href="/#projects">
          View projects
        </a>
        <a class="border border-ink/20 px-6 py-4 technical-label text-[0.74rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors hover:border-ink" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/tejas-kabra-0869aa291">
          LinkedIn
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell grid gap-14 py-20 md:py-28 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr]">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow text-signal">Profile</p>
      <h2 class="mt-6 text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.055em]">Who I am</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-9 text-ink/68">
      <p>
        Most of my work sits between electrical design and system integration. I like projects where
        the schematic, PCB layout, firmware, power tree, connectors, and mechanical constraints all
        have to work together before the system is useful.
      </p>
      <p>
        At Texas A&amp;M Formula Electric, I designed a 4-layer STM32G4 telemetry board with CAN, UART,
        power regulation, and a Quectel EG25 LTE modem. That project has shaped the way I think about
        hardware because it had to move from layout to firmware to bench testing to vehicle integration.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m also a Craig and Galen Brown Engineering Honors student, part of Texas A&amp;M RoboMasters,
        and have interned in electrical design for modular data center cooling infrastructure at
        Southland Industries.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y hairline bg-panel/45 py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="shell grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="border p-7 hairline">
        <span class="technical-label text-signal">01</span>
        <h3 class="mt-10 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.045em]">What I build</h3>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-ink/62">
          Embedded boards, CAN and LTE telemetry systems, power electronics, robotics hardware, and
          small electromechanical systems.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="border p-7 hairline">
        <span class="technical-label text-signal">02</span>
        <h3 class="mt-10 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.045em]">How I think</h3>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-ink/62">
          Start with constraints, design the full system, bring hardware up carefully, and use test
          results to make the next version cleaner.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="border p-7 hairline">
        <span class="technical-label text-signal">03</span>
        <h3 class="mt-10 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.045em]">What I want</h3>
        <p class="mt-5 leading-8 text-ink/62">
          A Fall 2026 co-op where I can contribute to electrical, embedded, hardware, or systems work
          that has to perform outside a classroom.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell grid gap-14 py-20 md:py-28 lg:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr]">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow text-signal">Purpose</p>
      <h2 class="mt-6 text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.055em]">Why I do this</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-9 text-ink/68">
      <p>
        Space has been the long-term motivation for me. I like the idea of building hardware for
        environments where the system has to work because there is no easy reset button.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m especially interested in the overlap between embedded hardware, robotics, and systems that
        could support people in extreme environments. Medical robotics for space applications is one
        version of that idea, and stories like <em>Project Hail Mary</em> are part of why that kind of
        engineering feels so interesting to me.
      </p>
      <p>
        Right now, the practical path is simple: get better at designing boards, writing firmware,
        testing real systems, documenting tradeoffs, and learning from engineers who have already
        shipped serious hardware.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="grid gap-10 border-t hairline pt-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_0.9fr] lg:items-end">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow text-signal">Current direction</p>
        <h2 class="mt-6 max-w-4xl text-5xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-0.055em] md:text-7xl">
          I’m trying to become the kind of electrical engineer who can own the path from idea to
          working hardware.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-ink/64">
        <p>
          I’m looking for work where the design has real constraints, the testing matters, and the
          result has to be reliable enough for other people to use.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 pt-3">
          <a class="border border-signal px-5 py-3 technical-label text-[0.74rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] text-signal transition-colors hover:bg-signal hover:text-panel" href={resumeHref}>
            View resume
          </a>
          <a class="border border-ink/20 px-5 py-3 technical-label text-[0.74rem] font-bold tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors hover:border-ink" href="mailto:kabratejas24@gmail.com">
            Email me
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
